Bugfix: Do not hang on a FIFO named like an exclusion tagfile

When `backup` ran with `--exclude-caches` or `--exclude-if-present name:header`,
and a directory contained a FIFO (or a symlink to one) with the name of the
exclusion tagfile, the backup hung forever and could not be canceled with Ctrl-C.

Restic now prints a warning for such a tagfile, does not exclude the directory
and continues the backup.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22182
